1. DEFINITIONS
==============================================================================

"Software" means the Grabber application, source code, scripts, modules, 
interfaces, query engines, adapters, documentation, and associated files 
authored or provided by Gabriele Vianello.

"Non-Commercial Use" means personal, educational, academic, and non-profit 
scientific research use conducted without any direct or indirect monetary 
compensation, financial gain, or commercial advantage.

"Commercial Use" means any use of the Software, in whole or in part, directly 
or indirectly, by or on behalf of a for-profit entity, corporation, partnership, 
sole proprietorship, or individual, that generates revenue, provides commercial 
services, supports commercial operations, or is intended for commercial gain.

"Commercial Analytics" means the execution of queries, filtering, aggregation, 
parsing, transformations, data mining, inspections, or extractions on any dataset 
(public, private, governmental, or proprietary) for the purpose of business 
intelligence, corporate decision-making, commercial consulting, commercial market 
research, competitor analysis, paid auditing, client deliverables, or any 
revenue-generating activity.

